# Supplemental Terms and Game Output Permission

These terms are supplied by Hexxis Studios. The additional permissions below control where they are broader than the PolyForm Noncommercial terms above. They do not restrict third-party rights or rights previously granted under Apache-2.0.

## 1. Your games and assets

Every person and organization, including a commercial studio, may use and modify VoxShop to create, test, build, publish, distribute and sell their own original games, models, artwork and other authored content (Game Output), for any purpose, without royalties, a separate commercial agreement, or mandatory VoxShop game branding or credit. Hexxis Studios claims no ownership of your original Game Output.

You may reproduce, modify and distribute the VoxShop runtime portions needed to play that Game Output, in source or compiled form, as part of the Game Output. Recipients may install, run and copy those runtime portions as necessary to play the Game Output. Preserve the included software license URLs and copyright/dependency notices in the distributed files; no player-facing credit screen is required.

Game Output can include normal in-game building, editing, modding and user-generated-content features. This permission does not cover distributing or hosting VoxShop, its editor, or a derivative engine as a standalone or general-purpose game-development product or service. Wrapping the editor in a nominal game or removing its branding does not turn engine distribution into Game Output.

## 2. Engine distribution and monetization

Except for the Game Output Permission, commercial use of VoxShop itself or a derivative engine/editor requires a separate written agreement from Hexxis Studios. This includes selling or sublicensing the engine/editor, bundling it into a paid development product, charging for access to a hosted authoring service, or operating an ad-supported authoring service. Internal use to create Game Output is expressly allowed by section 1.

Free public redistribution and noncommercial forks must retain this license and the Required Notice, prominently acknowledge VoxShop by Hexxis Studios with a link to https://github.com/Hexxis-Studios/voxshop in the running editor's About/Settings area and its download page, and identify modifications. Publicly distributed modified engines/editors must provide their complete corresponding source at no charge under these same terms. These requirements apply to the engine/editor, not to Game Output.

## 3. Product names and artwork

VoxShop, Hexxis Studios, the original VoxShop logo and derived product icons are reserved branding. You may retain them in accurate unmodified copies. Public modified engines/editors must use their own product name and logo, retain the attribution required above, and must not imply official endorsement. Descriptive references and required notices are permitted. This section does not claim ownership of users' game names, logos or assets.

## 4. Contributions and other licenses

Contributions intentionally submitted for inclusion are offered on these same terms unless separately agreed in writing; their authors retain ownership. Required dependency notices and their original licenses remain in force. These terms provide no permission to remove a dependency's notices or restrict separately licensed code.

For a separate commercial engine agreement, contact Hexxis Studios through https://hexxis-studios.github.io/. Donations to Hexxis Studios do not grant additional engine-distribution rights.
